  "result": "Perfect! All 157 tests pass. I've successfully created a dates module for consistent UTC date handling:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/dates.js** \u2014 New module with UTC date functions:\n   - `isValidDate(text)` \u2014 Validates YYYY-MM-DD format and real dates (moved from invoices.js)\n   - `addDays(date, n)` \u2014 Adds n days to a date (supports negative for subtraction)\n   - `daysBetween(a, b)` \u2014 Calculates whole days between two dates (b - a)\n   - All functions work in UTC, never local time\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Updated to use dates module:\n   - Removed local `isValidDate` function\n   - Imported `isValidDate` from `dates.js`\n   - `createInvoice` now uses the centralized date validation\n\n3. **test/dates.test.js** \u2014 Comprehensive test coverage (23 tests):\n   - **isValidDate tests** (8 tests):\n     - Valid dates in various formats\n     - Invalid formats (wrong separators, wrong order)\n     - Invalid dates (Feb 30, Apr 31, etc.)\n     - Leap year handling\n     - Edge cases (null, undefined, empty strings)\n   \n   - **addDays tests** (8 tests):\n     - Positive day increments\n     - Negative day increments\n     - Month/year boundary transitions\n     - Zero and large increments\n     - Leap year transitions\n   \n   - **daysBetween tests** (7 tests):\n     - Positive and negative differences\n     - Same dates (zero)\n     - Month/year boundaries\n     - Full year periods\n     - Inverse operation verification\n     - Leap year date intervals\n\nAll 157 tests pass. The dates module provides a centralized, UTC-aware date handling layer for the invoicing system.",
